I'll help you implement a typing animation effect for form inputs. Here's a clean, accessible solution using CSS and JavaScript:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Form with Typing Animation</title>
    <style>
        .form-group {
            margin-bottom: 20px;
            position: relative;
        }

        .form-label {
            display: block;
            margin-bottom: 5px;
            font-weight: 500;
            transition: all 0.3s ease;
        }

        .form-input {
            width: 100%;
            padding: 12px;
            border: 2px solid #ddd;
            border-radius: 4px;
            font-size: 16px;
            transition: border-color 0.3s ease;
        }

        .form-input:focus {
            outline: none;
            border-color: #007bff;
        }

        /* Typing animation */
        .typing-animation {
            display: inline-block;
            width: 2px;
            background-color: #007bff;
            animation: blink 1s step-end infinite;
            margin-left: 2px;
        }

        @keyframes blink {
            50% { opacity: 0; }
        }

        /* Input with typing indicator */
        .input-with-typing {
            position: relative;
        }

        .typing-indicator {
            position: absolute;
            right: 10px;
            top: 50%;
            transform: translateY(-50%);
            font-size: 12px;
            color: #666;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <form id="myForm">
        <div class="form-group">
            <label for="name" class="form-label">Name</label>
            <div class="input-with-typing">
                <input type="text" id="name" class="form-input" placeholder="Enter your name">
                <span class="typing-indicator" id="name-typing"></span>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="form-group">
            <label for="email" class="form-label">Email</label>
            <div class="input-with-typing">
                <input type="email" id="email" class="form-input" placeholder="Enter your email">
                <span class="typing-indicator" id="email-typing"></span>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="form-group">
            <label for="message" class="form-label">Message</label>
            <div class="input-with-typing">
                <textarea id="message" class="form-input" rows="4" placeholder="Enter your message"></textarea>
                <span class="typing-indicator" id="message-typing"></span>
            </div>
        </div>
    </form>

    <script>
        document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function() {
            const formInputs = document.querySelectorAll('.form-input');

            formInputs.forEach(input => {
                const typingIndicator = document.getElementById(input.id + '-typing');

                // Add typing event listener
                input.addEventListener('input', function() {
                    // Show typing indicator
                    typingIndicator.textContent = 'Typing...';

                    // Clear any existing timeout
                    if (this.typingTimeout) {
                        clearTimeout(this.typingTimeout);
                    }

                    // Set timeout to hide indicator after user stops typing
                    this.typingTimeout = setTimeout(() => {
                        typingIndicator.textContent = '';
                    }, 1500);
                });

                // Add focus/blur effects
                input.addEventListener('focus', function() {
                    this.parentElement.classList.add('focused');
                });

                input.addEventListener('blur', function() {
                    this.parentElement.classList.remove('focused');
                });
            });
        });
    </script>
</body>
</html>
```

This implementation provides:

1. **Typing Indicator**: Shows "Typing..." text when user is actively typing
2. **Auto-Hide**: Indicator disappears after 1.5 seconds of inactivity
3. **Focus States**: Visual feedback when inputs are focused
4. **Responsive Design**: Works on all screen sizes
5. **Accessibility**: Proper labels and semantic HTML

Key features:
- Clean, modern styling
- Smooth transitions
- No external dependencies
- Lightweight implementation
- Works with text inputs and textareas

To use this in your project:
1. Copy the HTML structure
2. Adjust the CSS variables to match your design system
3. Modify the JavaScript timing values as needed
4. Add more form fields by following the same pattern

The animation is subtle and enhances UX without being distracting. The typing indicator provides clear feedback that the system recognizes user input.

